WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:06.529
Speaker 1: There is a new report from Axios
reporter Jonathan Swan, which tells the story

00:00:06.529 --> 00:00:11.990
of a Donald Trump temper tantrum in which,
after losing the twenty twenty election, Trump

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.230
tried to just pull troops from around the
world.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:19.210
Now, you might think, that's great, I want
to bring our troops home.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.890
We shouldn't have troops all over the world
the way that we do.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:27.750
And I would agree with you, but this was not
a foreign policy calculation by Donald Trump.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:33.060
This was not a well crafted decision to reduce
the military presence around the world.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:42.380
This was not a calculated and much discussed
strategy for reducing the spread of the American

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.040
military throughout the globe.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.380
This was a temper tantrum over losing the
election on November 9th of twenty twenty.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:53.240
You might remember, that's the day after the
media finally said, OK, Joe Biden won.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:01:00.090
John McEntee, one of Donald Trump's favorite
aides, gave a note to Army Colonel Colonel

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.240
Douglas MacGregor.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:09.110
And on that note, it said, this is what the
president wants you to do, get us out of Afghanistan,

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:15.140
get us out of Iraq and Syria, withdraw completely
from Germany and get us completely out of

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.140
Africa.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.740
And McGregor explained, you know, we can't
really just do this by January 20th.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.320
And I certainly just can't do it by myself.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.750
And McKenty said to MacGregor, well, do what
you can.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:32.360
And McGregor said, I really can't do anything
I need, like a real order from the president.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.909
I can't just go and pull all of our troops
from around the world two days later.

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:39.520
And this is all based on Jonathan Swan's Axios
reporting.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.600
Such a letter was delivered to the acting
secretary of defense, Christopher Miller.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.780
All U.S. military forces are to be withdrawn
from Somalia by December 31st.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:55.580
All U.S. forces are to be withdrawn from Afghanistan
by January 15th with similar unrealistic dates.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:58.250
And Miller wondered, what the hell is going
on here?

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:02.290
The Department of Defense called the White
House a lawyer, Patrick Maloney, and asked

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:03.990
what is going on here?

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.510
They called Trump's national security adviser,
Robert O'Brien.

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.319
No one had any idea what was going on.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:11.859
This wasn't a plan.

00:02:11.859 --> 00:02:12.859
This wasn't policy.

00:02:12.859 --> 00:02:16.170
This was just a very strange temper tantrum.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:20.900
And as Jonathan Swan writes for Axios, the
US government's top national security leaders

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:26.430
soon realized they were dealing with an off
the books operation by Trump himself.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.299
Ultimately, it didn't happen.

00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:33.019
But as you can see, this is not the action
of a president who wanted to do these things

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.040
because they were the right things to do.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.889
If they were, he wouldn't have waited until
November 9th of the last year of his first

00:02:38.889 --> 00:02:39.889
term to do it.

00:02:39.889 --> 00:02:46.090
It was a triggered, tilted man, furious that
he lost, seemingly wanting to create as much

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:50.510
chaos as possible for Joe Biden, who would
be replacing him just two months later.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:56.419
And as Jonathan Swan writes, quote, Christopher
Miller told Associates he had three goals

00:02:56.419 --> 00:02:58.879
for the final final weeks of the Trump administration.

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:01.200
No one, no major war, No.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.340
Two, no military coup.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.340
And No.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:07.969
Three, no troops fighting citizens on the
streets of the United States.

00:03:07.969 --> 00:03:15.349
Think about the insanity of the situation
when the acting national security adviser,

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:21.279
acting secretary of defense, says my goals
for the lame duck period are preventing Trump

00:03:21.279 --> 00:03:26.890
from starting a war, preventing Trump from
using the military for a coup and preventing

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:31.680
Trump from deploying troops to fight citizens
on the streets of the United States.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:37.700
The more we read stories like this one, the
more we realize just how insanely close we

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.439
came to an even greater level of chaos.

00:03:41.439 --> 00:03:47.749
The stuff that was apparently narrowly avoided
almost makes the January 6th insurrection

00:03:47.749 --> 00:03:51.189
look relatively mild in comparison.

00:03:51.189 --> 00:03:55.609
And between the riots and Trump trying to
overturn the election results and stay in

00:03:55.609 --> 00:04:00.799
power and on a whim saying pull all troops
from everywhere and having lawyers in and

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:06.670
talking about martial law or seizing voting
machines or whatever else, the stuff that

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.200
happened is bad enough.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:11.540
But look at all of the things we're learning
about that almost happened.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:16.900
And as I've said, when Donald Trump left,
it was way worse than we knew over time.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:17.900
Where?

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:23.550
Going to learn more, but I don't know that
will ever really learn the full scope of exactly

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:24.810
how bad it was.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.430
And this is just yet another thing.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:31.470
And I know that, you know, there are probably
going to be people in my audience.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.460
I've already seen it in other enclaves.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.909
There's probably some people in my audience
who maybe identify with what is sometimes

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:42.699
called the revolutionary left, who will say
this was Trump outflanking the left on the

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:45.800
spread of the American military.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:49.420
Trump was trying to pull troops from all these
places that troops arguably shouldn't even

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.420
be in.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:55.060
And now leftists like David Pakman are saying
that it was a bad idea.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.860
I'm not saying it was a bad idea.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.741
And I've been arguing for drawing down troops
in Germany and in many other places for a

00:05:00.741 --> 00:05:02.199
decade on this program.

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:04.310
The point is, this wasn't policy.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:07.100
This was the day after the election was called
for.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:11.830
Biden, Trump, without consulting with anyone
and for no strategic reason, for no well thought

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:17.150
out foreign policy reason just says I'm going
to create an S storm for lack of a better

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:20.930
term for Joe Biden and just start pulling
troops haphazardly.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.509
It is not policy.

00:05:22.509 --> 00:05:27.470
And this is not how anybody who is a thinking
individual would say it should be done.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.120
We should be drawing down troops.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.950
We should be reducing our military footprint.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.140
There's no question about it.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.140
But if you do it as policy, you don't do it
once.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:36.509
You're already a lame duck.

00:05:36.509 --> 00:05:37.509
That doesn't make any sense.

00:05:37.509 --> 00:05:38.099
And that's pathetic

